$DIR/main.p:44:15: cannot store &holder().p.x in p, which outlives the temporary
    &holder().p.x points into the temporary Holder that holder() returns. The
    Holder made at main.p:44 is a temporary: nothing keeps it, so its object is
    dropped at the end of the statement. A view of the object may be passed to
    calls in that statement but may not outlive it. At the end of the statement,
    the temporary is dropped, but p lives longer, so it would be left pointing
    at a value that has been dropped.
    The view does not own the memory it looks at. Nothing keeps the temporary
    after the statement, so a stored view would outlive the value that keeps its
    memory alive.
    Keep the owner in a variable, so that it lives until the end of its scope,
    and take the view through that variable:
        v := holder()
        ... v ...
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3009" for a longer explanation)
